  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A partner can stay in the business for the whole year and still have two different earning weights.\n\nWhy? Because the amount invested may change halfway through.\n\nThe fix is simple: split the timeline into stages, calculate each stage, then add.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A invests ₹10,000. After 4 months, A withdraws ₹2,000 and keeps ₹8,000 for the last 8 months.\n\nA's weight = 10,000×4 + 8,000×8 = 40,000 + 64,000 = 104,000.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The wrong shortcut is 8,000×12. That pretends the withdrawal happened on day one.\n\nA change affects only the months after the change.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
